---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Searched from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/Searched.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import searched from "../data/searched.json";
const done = searched.filter((r) => r.status === "done").map((r) => [r.when, r.source, r.scope, r.result]);
const notyet = searched.filter((r) => r.status !== "done").map((r) => [r.source, r.scope, r.result]);
import fmp from "../data/findmypast.json";
import P from "../components/P.astro";
---
<Base title="What Has Been Read" eyebrow="And what has not"
      dek="A search that found nothing is still a result: it stops the next person repeating it. This page records both what has been done and what is still outstanding.">

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">FindMyPast — a six-day trial, spent</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">What a paid subscription was actually worth here</h2>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <p>The trial expires on 16 September 2026, so it was swept systematically rather than browsed.
      <strong>It is recorded in full, negatives included</strong> — the most useful thing a search can
      do for the next person is stop them repeating it, and two of the negatives below would
      otherwise cost someone a subscription to discover.</p>
      <div class="rec" style="margin-top:18px">
        {fmp.map((r) => (
          <>
            <div class="k">{r.kind.toLowerCase()}</div>
            <div class="v"><strong>{r.what}</strong> — {r.result}</div>
            <div class="w"></div>
          </>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h3 style="margin-top:1.8rem;margin-bottom:.6rem">The find: the family's New York parish</h3>
      <p>Two of Rocco Arena and Generosa Costa's New York children were baptised at
      <strong>Our Lady of Loretto</strong> — <P n="Sarafina Arena" /> in 1898 and Clementina in 1901.
      Loretto was <em>the</em> Italian parish of Little Italy, on Elizabeth Street, a few minutes'
      walk from the <strong>Mulberry Street</strong> address the 1899 manifest gives for Rocco.</p>
      <p>So the archive now knows not just the street but the church. <strong>The transcripts are
      locked</strong> behind a tier above the trial — and they would carry the
      <strong>godparents</strong>, who in an Italian parish are almost always kin. That is the single
      most valuable thing still sitting behind a paywall.</p>
      <h3 style="margin-top:1.8rem;margin-bottom:.6rem">The negative worth most</h3>
      <p><strong>The "Italy Births, Marriages and Deaths 1806–1900" sets do not cover Scilla.</strong>
      The test was clean: <strong>zero Polistena</strong> across all three, for a surname with six
      emigrants in the Ellis Island index alone. They are FamilySearch-derived and their Italian
      coverage runs to Sicily and the north, not Reggio Calabria. Anyone hoping to shortcut the
      Antenati work through a subscription site should know that before paying.</p>
      <p>The same sets were tried for the archive's oldest Sicilian question —
      <P n="Rosario Mazza" />'s marriage to Leonarda Bonanno, about 1870. <strong>No Leonarda Bonanno
      marriage exists in the set</strong>, and no Mariano Mazza birth, though 110 Nicotra marriages
      show it does reach the Catania area. That question stays where it was.</p>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:20px"><strong>Method, for whoever comes next.</strong>
      FindMyPast's search runs on a GraphQL endpoint —
      <code>POST /titan/marshal/graphql</code>, <code>recordSearch(filters, order, pageNumber)</code>
      under <code>root {"{"} search {"}"}</code>. Driving that directly turns a twelve-page click-through
      into one loop, and the <code>RecordMetadataId</code> filter restricts a search to a single
      record set. The whole sweep above cost a few minutes rather than an afternoon.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <h2>Everything read, and everything still to read</h2>
    <p class="dek" style="margin:.7rem 0 0">No Italian civil register has been opened for this
    family. That is the honest headline of this archive on the day it was built.</p>
    <Searched u={u} nil={["not-yet", "outstanding"]}
      rows={searched.map((r) => ({
        when: r.when, src: r.source, what: r.scope, got: r.result, outcome: r.status,
      }))} />
    <p style="margin-top:24px"><a href={u("/open-questions/")}>The questions each of these would answer →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
